# What the woltrust of tools/woltrust.rev can do beyond fe64176, one word per line (TRUST-core-4, chat 7293):
#   class            certificate bodies carry "class":"origin"|"trusted" and a trusted one "origin_cert"
#   statements       `woltrust sign --purpose release` (label wolos/release/1): signed release statements
#   withdrawn-version revocation entries with reason withdrawn-version (by statement serial)
# 68b5a03 (trust phase 4) reads class/origin_cert and withdrawn-version; its command line has no --purpose release yet
# (crypto::Purpose::Release exists, bin/woltrust.rs purpose() does not take it), so statements stay off.
# Add a word here in the same commit that moves woltrust.rev to a commit that has it.
class
withdrawn-version
